0231: a start after a crash or a kill keeps the shader caches

The crash journal (0017) treated every unclean end as a crash. Killed in the first seconds of
play (the startup phase lasted 300 frames) or during the startup hold with no pipeline in flight,
the next start deleted both caches and compiled everything again (297 s with Enhanced lighting
Ultra here); killed while compiling, the configs in flight became crash suspects, were left out
of the precache (compiled in play instead), and one in flight for two render target layouts was
counted twice and refused for good.
- aurora_pipeline_cache_note_crash() (the application's crash handler) sets a flag in the mapped
  journal. An unclean end without it (closed or killed) keeps the caches and records no suspects.
- Real crashes: suspects are counted once per config and still precached (a suspect that builds
  fine is lifted, as before); the caches are reset only on the third startup crash in a row.
- The startup phase ends 30 frames after the precache is done (was 300).
- No whole-file quick_check of dawn_cache.db (entries are verified by checksum as they are read,
  corruption errors on access reset it); the background prefetch also runs after an unclean exit.
  AURORA_CACHE_QUICK_CHECK=1 for testing.
- Stats prevExit (0 clean, 1 closed or killed, 2 crashed) and cachesReset for the hold screen.

